Applied by tools/build-toolchain.sh to bebbo/newlib-cygwin commit
0909ae9abc18b38595425143e7a63d9e2fc31174.  Commit 120371e changed __argv
from an array to a pointer to fix amiga-gcc issue #8, but crt0 retained two
writes through the pointer before the command-line initializer assigned it.
Both startup paths consequently write a longword through address zero.

Follow libnix's ownership model instead of giving the bad writes private
backing storage: crt0 only captures the OS startup state, while
__nocommandline constructs __argc/__argv during the init list.  An application
which overrides that hook gets its documented no-argument state, main(0,
NULL), from BSS initialization.

The shared header is part of the fix.  The array/pointer regression crossed a
translation-unit boundary, so keeping independent declarations would permit
the same defect again.  It also corrects the existing incompatible
_WBenchMsg definitions, which -flto -Wlto-type-mismatch diagnoses.  Mark the
link anchor used because an optimized standalone crt0 build otherwise removes
it and fails to pull the default parser from libc.

